# interplay_lifetime_suspend_held_record_rewritten: An exec that copies buffer X out is held on the gate when the host suspends; rvg_device_finish_suspend abandons its wait and tears every task down. While suspended the guest points X's entry at another page and moves a heap buffer's record to another offset. On the fresh device the exec is parsed again and waits again (as in interplay_life_suspend_blocked); released, it makes X and the heap buffer from the records as they are now: it reads the other page, and the heap buffer at its new offset. Nothing of the old records survives the resume.
